# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Secrets & credentials (keep .env.example files)
.env
google-services.json

# API — runtime data
api/uploads/
api/.hf-cache/

# Client — Expo / generated native projects (recreated by `npx expo prebuild`)
.expo/
.expo-shared/
client/android/
client/ios/

# Build output
dist/
dist-check/
*.log

# Local tool settings (permission allowlists accumulate per-machine paths)
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent skills installed by `npx skills add` (Higgsfield et al).
#
# Local dev tooling, not app code — but they must also stay out of the EAS
# upload, not just out of git. EAS archives from the *git root* (to support
# monorepos) even though eas.json lives in client/, and .claude/skills/* are
# Windows junctions pointing into .agents/skills/*. Recreating those links in
# EAS's temp clone needs privileges Windows does not grant by default, so the
# build dies with `EPERM: operation not permitted, symlink ...` during
# "Compressing project files".
.agents/
.claude/skills/
skills-lock.json

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
